WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.989 --> 00:00:07.100
The Tales of Dunk and Egg is a prequel series
set 90 years before A Game of Thrones.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:13.629
Dunk is a young knight – not a fancy noble
knight, but a humble travelling hedge knight.

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:20.390
He’s not very smart or skilled but he’s
tall and strong and determined to do what’s

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.390
right.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:28.939
His squire is a boy called Egg, who is secretly
a Targaryen prince, and future king of Westeros.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:34.110
In their first book, The Hedge Knight, Dunk
and Egg teamed up and fought a villainous

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.110
prince.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.340
For the next couple years, Dunk and Egg travelled
around Westeros – they went down to Dorne,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:45.290
fought some pirates, and visited Egg’s brother,
a young Maester Aemon, at Oldtown.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:51.190
So now in the second book, The Sworn Sword,
Dunk and Egg are a bit older, and more experienced,

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.760
but they’ve still got a lot to learn.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:00.100
The Sworn Sword was adapted to a graphic novel
with art by Mike S. Miller and Mike Crowell.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.830
In the previous book, Westeros enjoyed peace
and prosperity in spring time.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:10.370
But now, it’s a hot oppressive summer, and
Westeros is in “turmoil".

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.500
Cause the king, Daeron Targaryen, has died
in a plague.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.880
And his beloved son and heir Baelor, tragically
died in the previous book, [partly because

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:19.880
of Dunk].

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:20.939
So now Daeron’s second son, Aerys, is king.

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:22.729
[Aerys the First, not the Mad King Aerys the
Second].

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:28.049
And Aerys is a weak ruler – he’s more
interested in dusty old books than in being

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:29.049
king.

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:33.020
So Aerys lets his uncle, Brynden Rivers, run
the kingdom.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:38.950
Brynden, called Bloodraven, is a Targaryen
bastard with a reputation for sorcery and

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.950
spying.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:45.969
He eventually becomes the three-eyed crow,
teaching magic to Bran Stark 90 years later.

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:51.610
But in The Sworn Sword, Bloodraven is Hand
of the King, ruling Westeros with an iron

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.610
fist.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:57.250
When the plague hit King’s Landing, Bloodraven
had thousands of corpses piled up and burned

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:02.210
with wildfire, and the whole city glowed green
in the night.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:07.450
Now there are ironborn raiding the coast,
and a terrible drought, and across the narrow

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:12.770
sea, Bloodraven’s half-brother Bittersteel
is plotting invasion with the Blackfyres,

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.370
after a failed rebellion fifteen years ago.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:21.970
Meanwhile, Prince Maekar, the father of Aemon
and Egg, sulks in his castle at Summerhall.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.210
So these are troubled times, and tensions
are high.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:32.330
As a hedge knight, Dunk travels around Westeros,
working for whoever needs his sword.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:37.420
So in The Sworn Sword, he and Egg serve a
knight called Eustace Osgrey, who has a bit

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.260
of land and a tower called Standfast.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:46.220
Eustace is a sad old man, who lost his family
to war.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.040
Fifteen years ago, Eustace and his sons fought
in the Blackfyre Rebellion, when Bittersteel

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.150
and Daemon Blackfyre tried to take the throne
from their half-brother King Daeron.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.740
At the Battle of the Redgrass Field, Daemon
was killed in a rain of arrows from Bloodraven.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.790
Bloodraven fought a duel with Bittersteel,
and lost one of his eyes.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:11.340
Bittersteel and the surviving Blackfyres fled
from Westeros, to rebel again later.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.960
Eustace’s sons died in this battle.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.970
And his wife committed suicide [and his daughter
died in the plague].

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:23.340
Eustace says the death and carnage of the
battle was terrible – but he also describes

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.880
the beauty of the sunset over the Redgrass
Field.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:33.790
Eustace copes with his grief and loss by focussing
on the glory of the war – the brave warriors

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.920
and heroic battles.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.400
When he visits his family’s graves, Eustace
still toasts to the true king.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.860
He also keeps relics of his family’s history
– hundreds of years ago, the Osgreys were

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:51.380
a powerful house in the Reach, and Eustace
treasures these old memories [of this glorious

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.380
past].

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.810
Dunk and Egg discover that Eustace’s stream,
the Chequy Water, has gone dry – [and they

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.030
need that water in the drought].

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:02.790
Because Eustace’s neighbour, Lady Rohanne
Webber, built a dam upsteam to take the water.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:08.300
Eustace’s other knight, the mean-spirited
Ser Bennis, attacks one of Rohanne’s peasants

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.300
[escalating the conflict].

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.610
Eustace is furious that Rohanne took his water.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.970
He says Rohanne is a cruel murderer with “a
spider’s heart”.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:22.860
Known as the Red Widow, Rohanne is said to
be a witch who poisoned her four husbands.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:28.990
Rohanne’s castle, Coldmoat, was originally
an Osgrey castle – you can still see a faint

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.099
Osgrey lion beneath the Webber banners.

00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:36.409
Eustace won’t let the Red Widow take his
water, too.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:42.520
He wants to show his strength and pride, and
prove “that the chequy lion still has claws”.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:47.330
So he orders Dunk and Bennis to rally some
men and take back the stream.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:52.919
They get some peasants from Eustace’s villages,
and train them to fight, and they’re…

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:54.499
pretty much useless.

00:04:54.499 --> 00:05:00.740
Dunk and Egg realise that if these guys fight
the knights of Coldmoat, they’ll just die.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:06.479
So instead, Dunk goes to talk with Rohanne,
to convince her to give back their water.

00:05:06.479 --> 00:05:10.759
Dunk is a warrior who’s fought against knights
and pirates.

00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:15.430
But he’s nervous about talking to the highborn
lady, Rohanne.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.509
Dunk is just 19 years old [or 18], and he’s
awkward around women.

00:05:19.509 --> 00:05:25.240
So Prince Egg tells Dunk how to wear some
nice clothes and speak properly to the lady.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.180
At Coldmoat, Dunk meets Rohanne’s castellan,
Ser Lucas Inchfield.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:34.090
He’s called the Longinch because he’s
tall – but not as tall as Dunk.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:37.069
The Longinch is hostile and rude with Dunk.

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:41.699
He tricks Dunk into thinking that some random
other lady is Rohanne, just to fuck with him.

00:05:41.699 --> 00:05:45.639
But when Dunk meets the real Rohanne, she’s
not what he expected.

00:05:45.639 --> 00:05:52.150
She’s not an ugly old witch – she’s
a pretty young woman with a red braid and

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.310
freckles.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:58.770
Dunk greets her awkwardly, but Rohanne’s
playful and witty, and they have some chemistry

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.580
– and she agrees to a meeting.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:07.129
First, Dunk meets Septon Sefton, a drunk and
flatulent priest.

00:06:07.129 --> 00:06:11.539
He learns that Rohanne didn’t murder her
husbands, they were just older men who died

00:06:11.539 --> 00:06:16.939
of sickness, accident and war – two of them
died when Rohanne was a child.

00:06:16.939 --> 00:06:20.189
And now, Rohanne must marry again.

00:06:20.189 --> 00:06:24.379
Because according to her father’s will,
Rohanne only gets to keep Castle Coldmoat

00:06:24.379 --> 00:06:26.410
if she’s married within the next month.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:32.219
But she’s having trouble finding a good
husband – some men are put off by her reputation

00:06:32.219 --> 00:06:37.440
for murder, and others are intimidated by
the Longinch, who is determined to marry her

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:38.440
himself.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:42.909
Rohanne can’t get rid of the Longinch because
of her father’s will, and she fears he might

00:06:42.909 --> 00:06:44.370
marry her by force.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:49.939
There are also political rivals hoping to
take Rohanne’s land, watching for signs

00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:51.439
of weakness.

00:06:51.439 --> 00:06:57.500
Rohanne later says that as a young unmarried
female minor lord, she needs to show strength

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.319
to protect her power.

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:04.279
She knows this conflict with Eustace is a
meaningless pissing contest, but if she wants

00:07:04.279 --> 00:07:07.360
to rule, she can’t back down.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:13.039
So Rohanne demands that Eustace give her Bennis,
so she can punish him for hurting her peasant.

00:07:13.039 --> 00:07:18.589
And she refuses to take down her dam, cause
she needs the water for her crops, and her

00:07:18.589 --> 00:07:19.589
moat.

00:07:19.589 --> 00:07:22.849
And besides, the water is legally hers.

00:07:22.849 --> 00:07:27.580
Fifteen years ago, the king took the stream
from the Osgreys and gave it to House Webber.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:32.190
Because in the Blackfyre Rebellion, Eustace
wasn’t a loyalist fighting for King Daeron

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:36.309
– Eustace fought for the rebel, Daemon Blackfyre.

00:07:36.309 --> 00:07:41.529
Dunk discovers that the man he swore his sword
to is a traitor.

00:07:41.529 --> 00:07:47.000
Dunk makes one more appeal to Rohanne by bringing
up Eustace’s dead son, Addam, who Rohanne

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.330
had loved as a child.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:53.739
But it’s a sensitive topic – Rohanne blames
Eustace for Addam’s death in the rebellion

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:59.520
– so she gets angry, and slaps Dunk, and
threatens “Fire and sword”.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:05.069
Dunk and Egg go back to Eustace and ask why
he joined the Blackfyre rebels.

00:08:05.069 --> 00:08:09.439
He says that from his point of view, the Targaryens
were the traitors, and the Blackfyres were

00:08:09.439 --> 00:08:10.550
the loyalists.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:15.159
The Blackfyres believed that King Daeron was
an illegitimate bastard usurper.

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:19.990
They complained that he was weak, and that
he listened to women and Dornishmen.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:25.689
But Daemon Blackfyre was a powerful warrior,
legitimised by his father King Aegon the Fourth

00:08:25.689 --> 00:08:30.969
– and given the legendary sword Blackfyre,
the blade of the Conqueror.

00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:36.579
Eustace fought for the side he believed in,
and he says they almost won.

00:08:36.579 --> 00:08:41.061
If the Blackfyres had taken the Throne, they’d
be called the loyalists, and Daeron’s side

00:08:41.061 --> 00:08:42.580
would be the traitors.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:49.200
But since they lost, Eustace lives in defeat,
stripped of his lands and his family and his

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.230
pride, left with only memories.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.009
Dunk feels betrayed that Eustace misled him
into thinking he was a loyalist, and saying

00:08:57.009 --> 00:08:58.579
the stream was his.

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:04.029
So he decides to leave Eustace, but in the
night, Eustace’s forest called Wat’s Wood

00:09:04.029 --> 00:09:05.029
burns.

00:09:05.029 --> 00:09:08.930
It seems that Rohanne is carrying out her
threat of fire.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:13.880
So Eustace and Bennis rally their peasant
militia and plan to fight Rohanne.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:17.589
Dunk doesn’t want these innocent peasants
to be killed.

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:23.009
So he heroically sends the peasants home to
safety, and says he’ll end this conflict

00:09:23.009 --> 00:09:24.570
himself.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.149
Somehow.

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:31.410
Dunk and Egg and Eustace face off with Rohanne
and her men, with Rohanne wearing a super

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:34.279
cool spider-inspired outfit.

00:09:34.279 --> 00:09:39.790
Rohanne and Eustace refuse to back down – Rohanne
wants to punish Bennis, Eustace accuses Rohanne

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.660
of burning his woods, which she denies.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:47.060
The only way to end this with the lords’
pride intact is with blood.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:52.030
So Rohanne demands a trial by combat – and
Dunk fights the Longinch.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:57.040
The Longinch uses a two-handed poleaxe, and
both men are knocked into the stream.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:02.350
They beat each other up pretty bad, but in
the water, Dunk kills the Longinch.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:07.379
Dunk is badly injured, and he actually drowns
in the stream – luckily, Rohanne’s maester

00:10:07.379 --> 00:10:11.910
is ironborn, and knows how to resuscitate
a drowned man.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:16.100
And while Dunk recovers, Eustace and Rohanne
make peace.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.660
They bond over their memories of Eustace’s
son Addam.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:24.930
And Eustace and Rohanne get married – not
for love, but for political reasons.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:31.199
Cause marrying Rohanne makes Eustace the Lord
of Coldmoat – he finally gets back his family’s

00:10:31.199 --> 00:10:34.240
castle, restoring his Osgrey pride.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:39.020
For Rohanne, marrying Eustace means she gets
to keep her lands, in accordance with her

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:40.050
father’s will.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:43.589
And since Eustace is much older than her,
he’ll probably die soon – leaving her

00:10:43.589 --> 00:10:45.779
to rule for herself.

00:10:45.779 --> 00:10:50.620
So it’s a marriage of convenience that satisfies
both Rohanne and Eustace.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.690
But Dunk is bitter.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:58.529
It would’ve been nice if Rohanne and Eustace
made peace before Dunk nearly bloody died

00:10:58.529 --> 00:10:59.540
for them.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.360
And Rohanne never visited Dunk while he recovered.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:06.980
Dunk and Rohanne had a thing going, they were
flirting, Dunk had crazy trippy sex dreams

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:11.170
about her and everything, but she goes off
and marries the old guy??

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:15.450
To apologise, Rohanne offers Dunk a beautiful
well-bred horse.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:20.481
But Dunk says the horse is too good for him
– just like how Rohanne, as a highborn lady,

00:11:20.481 --> 00:11:23.140
is too good to be with Dunk.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:28.509
She insists on giving him something to remember
her by, so they share a passionate kiss, and

00:11:28.509 --> 00:11:31.060
he takes a lock of her hair.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:38.180
As Dunk and Egg ride north, a heavy rain falls
– welcome relief from this hot troubled

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.710
summer.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:46.180
So The Sworn Sword is not a battle of good
and evil, it’s about two pretty likeable

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:52.670
characters whose pride and politics draw them
into conflict – with Dunk once again putting

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:56.190
his life on the line to protect the innocent.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:02.069
And one of the recurring ideas in Dunk and
Egg is people not being who they seem.

00:12:02.069 --> 00:12:06.240
Egg is not a peasant boy, he’s a Targaryen
prince.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.009
Dunk isn’t technically a knight, cause he
was never knighted.

00:12:10.009 --> 00:12:14.509
Eustace is not a Targaryen loyalist, he was
a Blackfyre rebel.

00:12:14.509 --> 00:12:20.579
And Rohanne is not an evil old witch – she’s..
just a smart politician.

00:12:20.579 --> 00:12:26.200
She uses her reputation as a murderous “Red
Widow” as a political tool to intimidate

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.779
her rivals and protect her power.

00:12:28.779 --> 00:12:35.050
She’s not a monster – but she’s also
not innocent or naïve.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:40.750
Damming the Chequy Water is a major dick move,
even if she legally owns it – cause without

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:46.319
the Water, Eustace’s villages’ crops will
die, for the sake of Rohanne’s moat and

00:12:46.319 --> 00:12:47.880
her own crops.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:52.339
And Rohanne did once drown one of Eustace’s
men for stealing sheep.

00:12:52.339 --> 00:12:55.490
Rohanne can be ruthless… and cunning.

00:12:55.490 --> 00:13:00.950
Cause this conflict works out really well
for her – she proves her strength by not

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:02.079
backing down.

00:13:02.079 --> 00:13:05.350
She gets rid of the Longinch, who was a big
problem for her.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.630
She gets a husband, so she’ll keep Coldmoat,
but Eustace is old so she’ll rule by herself

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:10.630
soon.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:15.329
Everything goes so well for her that it’s
almost like she planned this.

00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:20.610
Rohanne says she didn’t burn Wat’s Wood,
that it must have been a natural accident.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:27.029
But it’s a pretty big coincidence that the
fire starts just after Rohanne threatened

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:28.029
“fire”.

00:13:28.029 --> 00:13:32.100
She even kinda admits that one of her men
might’ve started the fire.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:37.370
And the fire leads to this confrontation where
Rohanne demands the combat where the Longinch

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.670
dies.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:44.000
One of the first things Rohanne asks Dunk
is “Are you as strong as you appear?”.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:49.019
Maybe she planned to use Dunk to kill the
Longinch all along, and started the fire to

00:13:49.019 --> 00:13:51.329
force this conflict.

00:13:51.329 --> 00:13:56.500
Maybe this was all a trap, like the web of
the spider on her sigil.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.230
Hell, maybe she did murder some of her husbands.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:03.350
She says she didn’t love them, and it seems
she’d rather rule by herself.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:08.220
We’re told that her third husband choked
on a chicken bone, and the fourth died in

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.029
the plague – but maybe she really did poison
them.

00:14:12.029 --> 00:14:14.589
We.. can’t know for sure.

00:14:14.589 --> 00:14:18.639
Rohanne is an ambiguous, layered character.

00:14:18.639 --> 00:14:23.920
Like any lord, she risks the lives of ordinary
people for her power, and yet she’s still

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:28.680
a sympathetic character, making the best of
a difficult situation.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:34.449
She illustrates the complex balance of power
and pride and moral compromise that you need

00:14:34.449 --> 00:14:37.069
to survive in politics.

00:14:37.069 --> 00:14:39.110
And Rohanne’s story continues.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:45.959
The World of Ice and Fire history book reveals
that years later, Rohanne outlived Eustace,

00:14:45.959 --> 00:14:47.069
and married again.

00:14:47.069 --> 00:14:53.139
And her sixth husband was Gerold Lannister,
[who becomes] the Lord of Casterly Rock.

00:14:53.139 --> 00:14:58.690
So Rohanne went from being a minor noble to
the wife of one of the richest and most powerful

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.670
lords in Westeros.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:06.779
She had four sons with Gerold, including Tytos
Lannister – the father of Tywin Lannister,

00:15:06.779 --> 00:15:09.689
who’s the father of Cersei Jaime and Tyrion.

00:15:09.689 --> 00:15:15.410
So Rohanne is the great-grandmother of these
Lannisters – maybe they inherited her political

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:20.160
skill – except for Jaime – and for Cersei
she’s drunk [which is all of Book 4].

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:26.130
But after she had her fourth son, Rohanne
“vanished under mysterious circumstances”.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:27.130
What happened?

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:32.639
Rohanne’s husband, Lord Gerold, is rumoured
to be a murderer – it’s said that he killed

00:15:32.639 --> 00:15:36.180
his niece and brother so he could be Lord
of Casterly Rock.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:41.319
But even if that’s true, those murders were
for ambition – why would Gerold murder his

00:15:41.319 --> 00:15:44.320
own “beloved” wife, the mother of his
children?

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:45.320
[Probably married her for love in the first
place].

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:50.290
What was their relationship like, and what
really happened to Rohanne?

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:52.199
Maybe Dunk and Egg were involved.

00:15:52.199 --> 00:15:58.230
Cause a few years after Rohanne disappeared,
Egg, all grown up, as a knight, fought in

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.430
a battle against some rebels.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:06.010
And two of Rohanne’s sons fought alongside
him, one as Egg’s squire.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:10.089
Egg’s father, King Maekar, died in that
battle.

00:16:10.089 --> 00:16:15.630
And since his eldest kids and grandkids were
all either drunk or mad or nerds or Egg or

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:20.199
dead or female, a council was called to decide
who should be the next king.

00:16:20.199 --> 00:16:24.930
And they chose Egg – he became King Aegon
Targaryen the Fifth.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:30.490
And part of what convinced the council to
choose Egg was the words and the gold of Lord

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.600
Gerold Lannister.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:36.499
Egg then chose Dunk to be Lord Commander of
his Kingsguard.

00:16:36.499 --> 00:16:41.839
So clearly, Gerold and Rohanne and their family
were somehow involved in Dunk and Egg’s

00:16:41.839 --> 00:16:45.480
later lives – it sounds like there’s a
story here.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.740
Maybe we’ll find out in a future Dunk &amp; Egg
book.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:53.260
The author George Martin has talked about
writing ten or twelve Dunk &amp; Egg novellas,

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.870
to tell their whole life stories.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:00.790
So maybe one day, we’ll find out the fate
of the Red Widow.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:05.210
Egg was an unusual king, because he cared
a lot about the common people.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:10.150
He gave the peasants new rights and protections,
and sent food to the poor and hungry.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:14.870
And you can see how this was influenced by
his adventures with Dunk in The Sworn Sword.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:20.029
Like, at first, Egg acts too proud to work
with peasants.

00:17:20.029 --> 00:17:25.250
But Dunk teaches Egg to respect the smallfolk
– they might not be as educated and noble

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:31.179
as a prince like him, but the smallfolk are
still people with their own pride and families

00:17:31.179 --> 00:17:34.870
and skills, and they deserve Egg’s respect.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:40.289
Egg also shows prejudice against bastards
– he heard that bastards are untrustworthy,

00:17:40.289 --> 00:17:42.230
and “born to betrayal”.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:47.450
But Dunk points out that Dunk is probably
a bastard – he grew up an orphan in Flea

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:52.700
Bottom, and his parents probably never married,
but that doesn’t make Dunk a bad person.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:57.840
With Eustace and Rohanne, Egg gets to see
both sides of a political conflict.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:02.929
Rohanne shows Egg that rulers are not always
what they seem – and a delicate balance

00:18:02.929 --> 00:18:07.220
between image and power and pride are needed
to rule.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:10.950
Eustace rebelled against Egg’s family, the
Targaryens.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:17.490
But Egg learns why Eustace did what he did,
and sees that treason and loyalty, good guys

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:21.680
and bad guys, sometimes depend on your perspective.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:29.090
Egg sees the long-term aftermath of the Blackfyre
rebellion, and the impact of Eustace and Rohanne’s

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.610
conflict on the common people.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:36.770
It’s a great lesson for a young prince to
start thinking about how to be a good ruler.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:42.250
His adventures with Dunk ultimately make him
a wiser and more compassionate king, unlike

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:47.000
his dysfunctional brothers who grew up in
luxury at King’s Landing or Summerhall.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:51.799
And that’s why Dunk insists on taking Egg
on the road as a hedge knight.

00:18:51.799 --> 00:18:58.240
Cause even the noblest proudest rulers should
have the humility and wisdom to stay grounded,

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:05.560
to respect the common man, and sometimes to
ride in the rain on an old horse.

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:10.120
After The Sworn Sword, Dunk &amp; Egg’s next
adventure is The Mystery Knight – a story

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:15.370
of conspiracy, secret identities, dragon eggs,
and Bloodraven.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:19.530
All three Dunk and Egg stories are collected
in A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms, read on

